 "_": "Guiding without blocking (Abel, Nov 15). Each entry is a regular-expression fragment, matched case-insensitively as a whole word or phrase, on the question as typed and with its accents taken off. `offTopic`: words of a question about something Mini does not help with (weather, sports, money, news, films); with one of them, a question is out of scope when nothing in it is about the Bible or its helps (a book, a reference, a help word, a word of `bible`, a key term of the packs, a Translation Academy title): keep Bible words (rain, bread, king, song) out of it. `weak`: greetings, thanks, 'how much', 'what time': taken out of the question, and out of scope only when nothing is left ('Hello!', 'Thanks', 'What time is it?'): 'hello, who is Naomi?' and 'how much is a denarius?' are answered. `bible`: words that make a question about the Bible whatever else it says. `translate` and `review`: the words of a person announcing a task on a book ('I am translating Titus 1', 'Estoy revisando Jonás 2'): with only the book (and a chapter) left once they are taken out, the app offers a path through it (pipeline.ts pathStart).",
